.TH FILESYNC 1 "March 2026" "" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
filesync \- map and sync files across git checkouts
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B filesync
.RI [ \-V | \-\-version ]
.br
.B filesync
.RI [ help | \-h | \-\-help ]
.br
.B filesync
.I subcommand
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B filesync
is a Bash CLI that keeps file mappings in a per-project
.B .filesync/
directory (configuration, repos, and file rows). It discovers the project by walking parent directories from the current working directory, similar to
.BR git .
With no arguments,
.B filesync
prints a short usage summary and exits.

The dispatcher resolves its install root via
.B BASH_SOURCE
and
.B readlink
or
.B realpath
so a symlinked
.B PREFIX/bin/filesync
still finds package
.B lib/
and
.BR share/ .

If the first argument begins with a hyphen and is not a known subcommand (for example
.BR \-\-dry\-run ),
it is passed to
.B sync
as if you had run
.BR "filesync sync" .
The same dispatch accepts the
.B s
alias.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the program version and exit.
.TP
.BR help ", " \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.PP
With a subcommand first, the same
.B \-h
and
.B \-\-help
flags print extended usage for that subcommand only (see each command below).
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.SS "Project setup"
.TP
.B init
.RI [ directory ]
Create
.B .filesync/
with default
.IR config.json ", " repos.json ", and " files.json
at the project root. Default directory is the current working directory.
.B init
does not walk parents; the given directory establishes the project root.
If
.B .filesync/config.json
,
.B .filesync/repos.json
and
.B .filesync/files.json
all already exist,
.B init
exits with an error; if only some exist, it creates whichever files are missing.
.TP
.B enable
Turn on file sync in merged config.
.TP
.B disable
Turn off file sync in merged config.
.TP
.B path-mode
.RI [ relative | absolute ]
With no argument, print the effective
.I path_mode
from merged config
.RI ( relative
or
.IR absolute ).
With an argument, set
.I path_mode
in
.BR .filesync/config.json :
.B relative
resolves each repo
.B path
under the project root;
.B absolute
uses
.B path
as a filesystem directory as-is.
.TP
.B progress
.RI [ hidden | bar | percent ]
With no arguments, print the effective
.I progress_display
value (merged package defaults and
.BR .filesync/config.json )
to standard output.
With one argument, store
.I progress_display
in
.BR .filesync/config.json :
.B hidden
disables TTY progress;
.B bar
draws the full bracket bar with counts on standard error;
.B percent
draws a compact
.RI [ NNN% ]
indicator (package default).
.SS "Inspect and sync"
.TP
.B check
Also
.BR c .
.RI [ \-\-repo= name ]
.RI [ \-\-file= fragment ]
.RI [ \-\-status= list ]
Verify mappings, refresh
.I files.json
row status, and update
.I last_check_at
in config. Optional
.BI \-\-repo=
filters to one repo by name.
.BI \-\-file=
matches rows where
.I local_path
or
.I repo_file_path
contains the fragment (substring).
.BI \-\-status=
matches rows by cached
.I sync_status
before recomputing selected rows.
Token rules match
.BR sync :
literal statuses,
.IR unset ,
.IR all ,
and
.I error
for any
.IR error_* .
Compares each local file to the clone rendered from the master copy (diff drives
.IR sync_status ).
Per-row status lines use the same layout as
.BR list-files :
.IR [ sync_status "] " repo " | " repo_file_path
with an optional local path arrow and
.B ⚠
comma-separated
.I check_marker_warnings
codes when needed (crossover, local missing
.IR kind=clone ", "
master missing
.IR kind=master ", "
etc.).
Codes are also stored in
.IR files.json ;
those situations are not fatal on their own.
If the master file cannot be rendered, the row is
.I error_master_marker
but the command exits successfully unless other blocking issues exist.
When standard error is a terminal,
.I progress_display
in merged config is not
.B hidden
(see
.BR progress ),
and at least 10 rows are in the configuration,
.B check
may draw a scanning progress indicator on standard error; per-row lines go to standard output, so output may not stay fixed on one line.
.TP
.B sync
Also
.BR s .
.RI [ \-\-repo= name ]
.RI [ \-\-file= fragment ]
.RI [ \-\-check ]
.RI [ \-\-dry\-run ]
.RI [ \-\-force ]
.RI [ \-\-showall ]
.RI [ \-\-status= list ]
.RI [ \-\-include\-detached ]
Copy from master repos into the project and update
.IR files.json .
Filters
.BI \-\-repo=
and
.BI \-\-file=
match
.BR check .
.B \-\-check
runs
.B check
first using matching
.BI \-\-repo= ,
.BI \-\-file= ,
and
.BI \-\-status=
filters; if that preflight fails, sync exits without copying.
By default only rows with unset,
.I sync_required
or
.I error_missing_local
status are considered; detached rows are skipped unless
.BR \-\-include\-detached .
.BI \-\-status=
overrides with a comma-separated list of
.I sync_status
tokens (any token may match): literals
.RI ( synced ", " sync_required ", " detached ", ...),
.I unset
for empty status,
.I all
for every status except
.IR detached ,
unless
.B \-\-include\-detached
is set or
.I detached
appears in the list,
.I error
for any status whose name starts with
.IR error_ .
.B \-\-dry-run
prints planned work without writing files or status.
.B \-\-force
overwrites a local file that lacks a clone marker.
When no
.B \-\-status
filter is given,
.B \-\-force
also selects
.I local_newer
and
.I conflict
rows so master replaces the local copy.
.B \-\-showall
prints a per-file line for rows that are already in sync with master; by default those lines are omitted (counts in the summary still include them).
Coupled sync requires a master marker on the repo file.
Per-file lines start with a result symbol, use the same
.IR repo " | " repo_file_path
layout as
.BR list-files ,
and end with a bracketed outcome
.RI ( e.g. "\fB[Synced]\fR", "\fB[Already in sync]\fR", "\fB[Dry-run]\fR" ).
Rows skipped by status filter or marker rules are printed in gray.
Like
.BR check ,
a TTY progress indicator on standard error may appear when scanning many rows; per-file sync lines go to standard output, so output may not stay fixed on one line.
If no repos are configured (for example
.I repos.json
is an empty array),
.B sync
exits with failure.
.TP
.B list-repos
Also
.BR lr .
.RI [ \-\-repo= name ]
List configured repos or details for one repo by name.
.B list-repos
accepts only
.BR \-\-repo= ;
it does not accept
.BR \-\-file= ", " \-\-status= ", or " \-\-include\-detached .
.TP
.B list-files
Also
.BR lf .
.RI [ \-\-repo= name ]
.RI [ \-\-file= fragment ]
.RI [ \-\-status= list ]
.RI [ \-\-include\-detached ]
List file mappings and cached status; run
.B check
to refresh status fields. Filters match
.BR check .
If filters match no rows,
.B list-files
prints nothing and exits successfully.
Optional
.BI \-\-status=
uses the same comma-separated tokens as
.BR sync
(including
.B \-\-include\-detached
with
.IR all ).
Non-empty
.I check_marker_warnings
for a row are summarized on the line after the status.
.SS "Mappings and repos"
.TP
.B add-file
Also
.BR af .
.I repo_name path_in_repo \fR[\fI:local_path\fR] \fR...
.RI [ \-\-mark\-master ]
.RI [ \-\-also= repo1,repo2 ]
Track files from a repo checkout into the project. Each path token is relative to the repo; append
.IB : local_path
when the project-relative path differs.
The repo file must carry a
.B kind=master
marker; if it has a different filesync marker (for example
.BR kind=clone ),
the command fails.
If the repo file has no filesync marker at all, the command fails unless
.B \-\-mark\-master
is given, in which case a master marker line is prepended (comment style follows the path extension).
The local file is written (or overwritten) with content rendered from the master copy including a
.B kind=clone
marker.
.B \-\-also=
mirrors the mapping into other initialized projects. Each value is a repo name from the current project's
.B repos.json
whose
.B path
points at a sibling project root containing its own
.BR .filesync/ .
For each sibling project, filesync uses that project's configuration (including
.BR path_mode )
and writes/overwrites the clone file under that sibling project's root.
.TP
.B add-master
Also
.BR am .
.I target_repo local_path \fR[\fI:path_in_repo\fR] \fR...
.RI [ \-\-also= repo1,repo2 ]
Promote local files into the master repo and add mappings. Omit
.IB : path_in_repo
when the master path matches
.IR local_path .
With
.BR \-\-also= ,
filesync mirrors mapping rows into sibling projects but initializes those mirrored rows as
.B sync_required
so each project can run
.B check
or
.B sync
to validate timestamps and status in its own context.
.TP
.B add-clone
.I target_repo master_path \fR[\fI:local_path\fR] \fR...
.RI [ \-\-also= repo1,repo2 ]
Add a
.B kind=clone
copy and
.I files.json
row in a sibling initialized project, using a
.B kind=master
file that lives under the current project root.
Each
.I master_path
token is project-relative; append
.IB : local_path
to write the clone at a different path in the target project (the clone marker
.B path=
still uses
.IR master_path ).
If the source file has no filesync marker, a
.B kind=master
marker is prepended automatically (comment style follows the path extension); other non-master markers are rejected.
The target project's
.B repo=
token and row
.B repo_name
are inferred from that project's
.B repos.json
by finding the repo entry whose configured checkout path resolves to this project root.
The command fails if the target local file already exists or if
.I files.json
already lists that
.IR local_path .
.B \-\-also=
mirrors the same operation into additional sibling projects (same rules as
.BR add-file ).
.TP
.B push
.RI [\-\-all]
.I local_path \fR[\fIlocal_path ...\fR]
Push local content to the master path in the linked repo.
With
.BR \-\-all ,
also pushes every mapping whose
.I sync_status
in
.I files.json
is
.BR local_newer ;
if no
.I local_path
arguments are given, only those rows are selected.
If both
.B \-\-all
and explicit
.I local_path
arguments are given, the union is pushed (each path once).
If
.B \-\-all
is given, no paths are listed, and there are no
.B local_newer
rows, the command exits successfully after a short notice.
.TP
.B detach-file
Also
.BR ddf .
.I local_path \fR[\fIlocal_path ...\fR]
Set
.I sync_status
to
.I detached
in
.IR files.json
and rewrite the first marker line in each local file to
.BR kind=detached
(keeping path/repo context when possible).
.TP
.B attach-file
Also
.BR daf .
.I local_path \fR[\fIlocal_path ...\fR]
Re-couple detached rows and run
.B check
on each.
.TP
.B detach-repo
Also
.BR ddr .
.I repo_name
For every row in
.I files.json
whose
.I repo_name
matches
.IR repo_name ,
run the same operation as
.BR detach-file
for that row's
.IR local_path .
.TP
.B attach-repo
Also
.BR dar .
.I repo_name
For every such row, run the same operation as
.BR attach-file
(non-detached rows are skipped as for
.BR attach-file ).
.TP
.BR rmf ", " remove-file
.RI [ \-\-all-missing ]
.I local_path \fR[\fIlocal_path ...\fR]
Remove the matching row(s) from
.IR files.json .
On disk, removes
.B kind=clone
or
.B kind=detached
marker line(s) from each local file; leaves
.B kind=master
lines so a shared master copy can stay valid for other projects.
.B \-\-all-missing
adds every mapping whose cached
.I sync_status
is
.BR error_missing_master
(union with any explicit
.IR local_path
arguments); if it is the only selector and there are no such rows, the command exits successfully after a short message.
.TP
.BR rmr ", " remove-repo
.I repo_name
.RI [ \-y " | " \-\-yes ]
Remove the named repo from
.IR repos.json .
If
.I files.json
has no rows for that repo, the repo entry is removed. If there are still file mappings for that repo, the command prompts for confirmation; if you agree, each such mapping is removed like
.BR remove-file ,
then the repo entry is removed. Local file contents are not deleted. Answer
.B n
or press Enter to abort without changes.
.B \-y
and
.B \-\-yes
skip that prompt (non-interactive / scripting).
.TP
.B add-repo
Also
.BR ar .
Interactively add a repo definition to
.IR repos.json .
.TP
.B edit-repo
Also
.BR er .
.I repo_name
.RI [ \-\-rename= name ]
.RI [ \-\-path= path ]
.RI [ \-\-url= url ]
.RI [ \-\-branch= branch ]
Edit a repo entry. Renaming updates
.I repo_name
in every
.I files.json
row and the
.B repo=
token in local clone/detached sync markers for those rows.
.SS "Self-update"
.TP
.B update
.RI [ \-y " | " \-\-yes ]
Compare the installed version with the latest GitHub release. If a newer release exists and this install can be upgraded automatically (a git checkout of filesync, or a matching
.B .deb
on the release), prompts whether to apply the update:
.B git
pull and
.B make install
from a clone, or
.B dpkg \-i
for the release
.B .deb
(uses
.B sudo
for
.B make install
and
.B dpkg \-i
when
.B sudo
is on
.BR PATH ,
otherwise runs them without elevation). If no update is needed, prints that and exits. If an update is available but cannot be installed automatically from this layout, prints a link to the release page.
.B \-y
and
.B \-\-yes
skip the confirmation prompt and apply immediately when an update is available.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I .filesync/config.json
Merged over package defaults; toggles, path mode, and
.I progress_display
.RI ( hidden \| bar \| percent )
for TTY progress on long loops.
.TP
.I .filesync/repos.json
Array of repo definitions.
.TP
.I .filesync/files.json
Array of file mapping rows.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B FILESYNC_PROJECT_ROOT
Project root directory.
.TP
.B FILESYNC_DIR
Path to the
.B .filesync
directory.
.TP
.B FILESYNC_INSTALL_PREFIX
For
.B "filesync update"
from a git checkout when applying an update,
.B PREFIX
passed to
.BR "make install"
when autodetection is wrong.
.TP
.B FILESYNC_VERBOSE
When set to a non-empty value, enables extra informational messages on standard error for commands that support it.
.TP
.B FILESYNC_NO_PROGRESS
When set to
.BR 1 ,
TTY progress is not drawn on standard error (overrides
.IR progress_display ).
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
When set to a non-empty value, disables ANSI color in terminal output.
.TP
.B FILESYNC_DEBUG
When set to a non-empty value, commands that use the standard runtime print a short debug line on standard error when a command fails under
.BR "set -e"
(errtrace).
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
.B 0
Success, or
.B check
/
.B sync
completed with nothing blocking (or file sync is disabled and the command exits after notice).
.TP
.B 1
Failure: missing dependencies, invalid or missing configuration, usage errors, or
.B check
/
.B sync
completed with blocking issues or failures. Messages on standard error are prefixed with
.B filesync:
where applicable.
.TP
.B 2
Reserved for auxiliary tooling (e.g. test runner scripts); the
.B filesync
CLI itself uses
.B 1
for invalid options on subcommands such as
.BR update .
.SH SEE ALSO
Extended configuration and environment notes live in
.I docs/configuration.md
in the source repository (the
.B .deb
package ships this manual page, changelog, and copyright; it does not install that Markdown file).
